First Principle Definition

Interviewer:

What is Docker?

Answer:

Docker solves the "it works on my machine" problem. Instead of shipping only application code, Docker packages the application along with its runtime, dependencies, libraries, and configuration into an image. That image runs as an isolated container on any machine with Docker installed, giving consistent behavior across development, testing, and production.

Interview Analogy

Interviewer:

Why not just install Node everywhere?

Answer:

Imagine every developer cooks the same recipe in a different kitchen. One kitchen has different ingredients, another has an older oven, another is missing tools. The same recipe gives different results.

Docker is like giving everyone the same fully equipped portable kitchen, not just the recipe.

