30-Second Interview Answer

"Docker is a containerization platform. Before Docker, applications often failed when moved between environments because OS libraries, runtime versions, and dependencies differed. Docker packages the application together with everything it needs into an image. That image runs as an isolated container, so the application behaves consistently on any machine. Compared to virtual machines, containers share the host OS kernel, making them much lighter, faster to start, and more resource-efficient."

Interviewer agar deep puch le:

Q: Docker Image aur Container me difference?

Image = Blueprint (read-only template).
Container = Running instance of that image.

Analogy: Image is like a class in OOP, and a container is like an object created from that class.
